# Route anthropic - a hosted model, reached only on the operator's terms

DECLARED 2026-10-02 (WHAT'S LEFT B18), on the operator's word: "backed by ollama as a first route
then secondarily through additional API as added" and "let's do what I said then, set up a second
set for parity, why not? I'm not scared of it." RULE 4 is amended for it, narrowly (CLAUDE.md), and
this record is the one place that says what the amendment reaches.

A route is a model reached somewhere other than the rack. A model with no route in its name is
Ollama's, as it always was; a model named `anthropic://<model>` is asked of the host below, in
Anthropic's messages form, by `manjuel/routes.py` and by nothing else.

WHAT LEAVES THIS MACHINE: the objective and the feed of a parity case the operator ran by name
(`/parity hosted`), after the run said what would leave and he said yes. Nothing else is sent: not a
seat's answer, not a file, not the record. Text the law gate would refuse as an objective, the client
tag, and the value of any secret in the environment are refused by name and never sent.

WHAT IT COSTS: the provider bills the operator, at its own prices (RULE 6: the operator authorises
the spend; no hand ever makes a hosted call).

WHAT TURNS IT ON: the key, `MANJUEL_ROUTE_ANTHROPIC_KEY`, in `.env`, put there by the operator. Without
it the route is OFF and nothing is sent. The key is read at the call, sent in one header, and never
printed, logged, stored or returned (RULE 7).

WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH: no seat sits on it (`us.py` reports one that names it), and it does not embed
or stream. It is https to another machine; a redirect is never followed.

`remote` is not taken on faith: `us.py` derives it from `base_url` and reports a record that says
otherwise. `can_approve` is false here as everywhere (RULE 6).

```json
{
  "adapter": "anthropic",
  "base_url": "https://api.anthropic.com",
  "can_approve": false,
  "covenant": "1512741580b7239b",
  "id": "route_anthropic",
  "kind": "route",
  "office": "MANJUEL",
  "remote": true,
  "reports_to": "manjuel",
  "source": "manjuel/routes.py",
  "us": 1,
  "wall": "https://api.anthropic.com, only while MANJUEL_ROUTE_ANTHROPIC_KEY is set; sends the objective and feed of a parity case the operator ran by name, and nothing else",
  "writes": false
}
```
